{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Authentication - One Okta Device Token Hash Across Many Accounts [table]",
	"Description": "Finds a single device token hash used to authenticate to several different accounts. One browser signing into three or more accounts is either a shared kiosk or one machine working through a list of stolen credentials.\n\nThreshold: 3 or more distinct accounts per device token hash. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_multiple_okta_user_authentication_events_with_same_device_token_hash/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "c83dc376-6113-5531-afa1-8b024160a825",
	"SearchReference": "da8352ea-e420-5137-a414-ab12d8e28d17"
}